From b6715e6fb05613f309c9b69c2e358e8c4077b3ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:11:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gbm: the player information publishes its sentence, badges,
 speakers and metadata levels

Publishes, as properties of the Home window and only when their value
changes (as the page has always been fed), what the new overview page and
its detail pages draw:

- hades.sum.state / code / arg / todo / more / head: the sentence at the top
  of the page, decided by KODI::UTILS::PLAYERINFO::Decide() from what the
  window system already knows (the reason that Dolby Vision is not native,
  the signal, why HDR is not told, pictures not shown in the last 10 s, the
  step-down level, the enhancement layer resynchronizing, the refresh rate
  against the video's, why the sound is decoded);
- hades.sum.vbadge and hades.sum.abadge: the text badges of the formats;
- hades.audio.spk: the speakers that the layout lights;
- hades.video.color / matrix / area, hades.src.mastering / cll,
  hades.out.ratefit, hades.play.dropped / skipped;
- hades.dv.l3 .. l255 and hades.dv.lvhead / lvfile / lvused / lvsent: the
  values of every metadata level and the table of which the file has, Hades
  acts on and the display is sent, for native output and for a picture
  rebuilt as HDR10 or SDR;
- hades.f.<name>: 1 for 750 ms (of the two beats a second) where the value
  of hades.<name> changed from one to another, for the values that are
  worth watching (not the counters that move with every beat).

All of it is computed only while the page is open (the Dolby Vision keys,
which skins may read at any time, are as cheap as before: a loop over the
blocks of the RPU), and every key is set empty when the page closes.
